{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Like the dew</b> — Rabbi Moses said: what is the meaning of 'Mount Hermon' for 'Mount Zion'?! And he explained it: like the dew of Hermon that is fitting to descend upon the mountains of Zion. And the correct in my eyes: that 'like the dew' serves as a connective, and so it is 'like the dew of Hermon' — like the dew that descends. And behold, he mentioned two things, by way of 'he will cover [?] and many like it, for the blessing is in the dew, then the produce increases, upon which the life of man depends.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 133, :notes {0 "The cited phrase 'יכפה אף ורבים כמוהו' is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The word 'אף' may be a corruption or abbreviation, and the syntactic construction is obscure in the witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:41.442258637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}